{"id": 21846, "group": "campus-iit-kanpur-placements", "sent_at": "2026-11-06T03:37:35.856126+00:00", "text": "it happened yesterday in iit bhu \n\n### Problem Statement\n\nYou are given a binary tree where each node contains an integer value.\n\nThe tree is represented using the following input format:\n\n- `N`: The total number of nodes in the tree.\n- `S`: The value of the root node.\n- `pos[N-1]`: An array of strings representing the positions of the remaining nodes relative to the root.\n- `val[N-1]`: An array containing the corresponding values of those nodes.\n\nEach position string consists of:\n- `L`: Move to the left child.\n- `R`: Move to the right child.\n\nFor example:\n```text\nN = 5\nS = 1\n\nL   4\nR   3\nLR  2\nRR  2\n```\n\nThis represents a binary tree with root value `1`, a left child with value `4`, a right child with value `3`, and so on.\n\n### Task\n\nFind the **sum of the values of all nodes that have exactly two children** (both left and right children).\n\n### Important Note\n\nThere was an incorrect test case in the original test data:\n\n```text\nn = 3\ns = 10\npos = [\"LL\", \"R\"]\nval = [5, 6]\n```\n\nThis test case is invalid because the node at position `LL` requires its parent at position `L` to exist. However, no node is provided at position `L`.\n\nThe test case should be corrected to ensure that every non-root node has all its ancestors present in the tree.", "author_tag": "BHU", "reply_to": {"id": 21726, "text": "what questions were asked in navi sde oa for kanpur?", "author_tag": "IITB"}, "attachment": null, "deleted": false}
